    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner (member) create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a `NOTIFY` logger** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:105`) \u2014 `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")`, sitting alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger and following the same \"well-known, separately named logger\" convention already used in this class.\n\n2. **Added `enqueueWelcomeNotification(Owner)`** \u2014 emits one `NOTIFY.info(...)` line containing both the owner id (`owner.getId()`) and the `memberId` (`owner.getMemberId()`).\n\n3. **Wired it into the create flow** via `createdOwnerResponse(...)`, right after the existing audit emitters \u2014 so it runs only after `saveOwner` succeeds and the generated id is populated.\n\nThe `NOTIFY` line is confirmed emitted (`NOTIFY - welcome notification enqueued for owner id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3`), and the full test suite passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
